- <h1>teamLab Barcelona: Is There One? (And What to Do Instead in 2026)</h1>
- <div class="article-meta"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marvynhalfon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Marvyn Halfon</a> &middot; Co-founder, SABDA Studio<br><span style="opacity:.72">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-08-13">August 13, 2026</time></span></div>
-<p>Short answer: no, Barcelona does not have a permanent teamLab museum. But the full answer is more interesting, because teamLab has exhibited here twice, pieces of that spirit are still in the city, and a few venues get surprisingly close to what makes teamLab special. Here is the complete picture.</p>
+ <h1>teamLab Barcelona: Is There One? (And What to See Instead in 2026)</h1>
+ <div class="article-meta"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marvynhalfon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Marvyn Halfon</a> &middot; Co-founder, SABDA Studio<br><span style="opacity:.72">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-22">October 22, 2026</time></span></div>
+<p>Short answer: no. There is no teamLab museum in Barcelona, and as of October 2026 teamLab has not announced any exhibition in Barcelona or anywhere else in Spain. teamLab Borderless and teamLab Planets are in other cities. But the full answer is more useful, because teamLab has exhibited here before, one teamLab work is still listed in the city, and a few venues get close to what makes teamLab special.</p>
+<hr />
 <h2>What happened to teamLab in Barcelona</h2>
-<p>teamLab, the Japanese art collective behind the immersive museums in Tokyo and the touring installations that fill every feed, came to Barcelona in 2021. CaixaForum hosted the exhibition teamLab: Art, Technology and Nature from May 2021 to January 2022, with two interactive works where visuals responded to visitors' movement. Around the same time, Moco Museum opened with teamLab pieces in its digital art rooms.</p>
-<p>The CaixaForum show ended in January 2022 and never returned. Since then, "teamlab barcelona" has been a search with no good answer. Until now.</p>
-<h2>The 4 closest things to teamLab in Barcelona right now</h2>
-<p>What people love about teamLab is a specific combination: digital nature, room-scale projection, and interaction, the art responds to you. No single Barcelona venue replicates all three, but each of these delivers part of it.</p>
-<h3>1. Moco Museum: the teamLab connection that stayed</h3>
-<p>Moco's digital immersive rooms in El Born have shown teamLab works, including pieces from the Moco Masters digital program, alongside Warhol, Banksy and Hirst. The rotation changes, so check what is currently on display, but this is the venue with an actual teamLab history in the city. Entry from about 16 euros. <a href="https://www.mocomuseum.com/tickets/barcelona/">mocomuseum.com</a></p>
-<h3>2. IDEAL: the room-scale spectacle</h3>
-<p>If what you want is the scale, a vast hall where projections cover every surface, IDEAL in Poblenou is Barcelona's biggest. It is spectator-style rather than interactive, and the current Tutankhamun exhibition (since March 2026) shows the format at full power. From 12.50 euros on weekdays. <a href="https://idealbarcelona.com/en/">idealbarcelona.com</a></p>
-<h3>3. SABDA: the participation</h3>
-<p>Full disclosure: this is our studio. What no other Barcelona venue offers is the third teamLab ingredient, being part of the work instead of watching it. SABDA is a 360-degree projection room with Dolby Atmos spatial audio in Eixample where you take yoga, sound healing and breathwork classes inside custom-designed visuals. You are not looking at the room, you are in it, moving through it, for a full hour. Classes from 18 euros. And from October 2026, the same room opens a new immersive art exhibition program. Details first at <a href="/exhibitions/">our exhibitions page</a>.</p>
-<h3>4. Eonarium: the atmosphere</h3>
-<p>Light shows projected inside a historic church, quieter and more contemplative than the big venues. Not interactive, but the closest thing in the city to teamLab's meditative side. <a href="https://eonariumexperiences.com/barcelona/en/">eonariumexperiences.com</a></p>
-<h2>What about the Van Gogh immersive experience in Barcelona?</h2>
-<p>Same story, different artist. Barcelona has hosted several Van Gogh immersive shows over the years, Meet Vincent Van Gogh, El Mundo de Van Gogh, and the touring Van Gogh: The Immersive Experience. They were all temporary, and they rotate in and out of the city. As of mid-2026 there is no permanent Van Gogh immersive show running in Barcelona: IDEAL, which hosted art-focused immersive shows in the past, is currently running Tutankhamun instead.</p>
-<p>If a Van Gogh show is the reason you searched, check IDEAL's current program first, then consider whether one of the venues above scratches the same itch. The format is identical, only the paintings change.</p>
+<p>teamLab, the Japanese art collective behind teamLab Borderless and teamLab Planets, has shown in Barcelona twice. CaixaForum Barcelona hosted "teamLab. Art, Technology and Nature" from 17 May 2021 to 9 January 2022, with interactive works that responded to visitors' movement. <a href="https://www.teamlab.art/e/caixaforum_barcelona/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">teamlab.art</a></p>
+<p>In October 2021, Moco Museum opened its Barcelona branch with a digital art programme that included teamLab's "Flowers and People – A Whole Year per Hour", a work where a year of seasonal flowers blooms and scatters over an hour and reacts to people standing in front of it. teamLab's own website still lists it at Moco Barcelona with no end date. <a href="https://www.teamlab.art/e/mocomuseumbarcelona/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">teamlab.art</a></p>
+<p>The CaixaForum show closed in January 2022 and has not returned.</p>
+<hr />
+<h2>The closest things to teamLab in Barcelona right now</h2>
+<p>What people love about teamLab is a specific mix: digital nature, room-scale imagery and interaction. No Barcelona venue does all three, but each of these delivers part of it.</p>
+<h3>1. Moco Museum: the teamLab connection</h3>
+<p>Moco's digital and immersive rooms in the Born are the only place in Barcelona where a teamLab work is still listed, alongside Studio Irma's mirrored infinity room "Diamond Matrix" and works by Banksy and KAWS. Moco notes that not every artwork is always on display, so if the teamLab piece is the reason you are going, ask at the desk. Tickets from €14.95, children up to 6 free. <a href="https://www.mocomuseum.com/barcelona/digital-immersive-art-museum-barcelona/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mocomuseum.com</a></p>
+<h3>2. SABDA's new immersive show: digital nature at room scale</h3>
+<p>Full disclosure: SABDA is our venue. SABDA's new immersive show is a 25 minute journey through four worlds of life on Earth, made in Unreal Engine and projected across the four walls of a 360° room with Dolby Atmos sound, for 25 people per session at C/ Muntaner 83B in the Eixample.</p>
+<p>Of everything in the city, it is the closest to teamLab's digital nature: you travel at animal eye level and, for 25 minutes, become one of them, with no headset. It opened on 17 October 2026 and runs on Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays, at €20 for adults and €12 for children, including a welcome glass of cava or juice in SABDA Café. It is not interactive in the teamLab sense. Details on <a href="/exhibitions/">our exhibitions page</a>.</p>
+<h3>3. Casa Batlló's Gaudí Cube: digital art in a Gaudí house</h3>
+<p>Every Casa Batlló ticket ends in the Gaudí Cube, a six-sided LED room where Refik Anadol presents "Gaudí Dreams". Different artist, similar wow. From €29, children up to 12 free. <a href="https://www.casabatllo.es/en/experience/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">casabatllo.es</a></p>
+<h3>4. Codi Gaudí: the interactive part</h3>
+<p>For interaction, Codi Gaudí at Espai Imagina uses VR headsets and mixed reality to let you walk through buildings Gaudí never built. Until 8 January 2027, about 70 minutes, closed on Tuesdays.</p>
+<h3>What about IDEAL?</h3>
+<p>IDEAL, the city's large projection venue, has nothing open this autumn: its Pompeii show closed on 21 September 2026 and no new exhibition has been announced.</p>
+<hr />
+<h2>What about Van Gogh?</h2>
+<p>Same story, different artist. No Van Gogh exhibition or immersive experience is running or announced in Barcelona. We cover the full answer, the Van Gogh shows the city has had, and where to see real Van Goghs in our guide to <a href="/blog/van-gogh-barcelona/">Van Gogh in Barcelona</a>.</p>
+<hr />
 <h2>The honest bottom line</h2>
-<p>Barcelona does not have a teamLab, but it has something no teamLab city has: a scene where you can watch immersive art at scale (IDEAL), see actual teamLab pieces in a museum (Moco), and then physically practice inside the projections (SABDA), all within 20 minutes of each other. We compared every option with real 2026 prices in our <a href="/blog/best-immersive-experiences-barcelona/">guide to the best immersive experiences in Barcelona</a>.</p>
+<p>Barcelona does not have a teamLab, and nothing is announced. What it has is one teamLab work listed at Moco, a new digital-nature show in a 360° room at SABDA, digital art at Casa Batlló and headset VR at Codi Gaudí, all within 20 minutes of each other. We compare every option with 2026 prices in our guide to the <a href="/blog/best-immersive-experiences-barcelona/">best immersive experiences in Barcelona</a> and our guide to <a href="/blog/digital-art-barcelona/">digital art in Barcelona</a>.</p>
+<hr />
+<h2>FAQ</h2>
+<p><strong>Is there a teamLab in Barcelona?</strong>
+No. There is no teamLab museum in Barcelona, and teamLab has not announced any exhibition in Barcelona or elsewhere in Spain as of October 2026.</p>
+<p><strong>Was teamLab ever in Barcelona?</strong>
+Yes. CaixaForum Barcelona hosted "teamLab. Art, Technology and Nature" from 17 May 2021 to 9 January 2022, and Moco Museum has shown teamLab's "Flowers and People – A Whole Year per Hour" since October 2021.</p>
+<p><strong>Is there teamLab Borderless or teamLab Planets in Barcelona?</strong>
+No. teamLab Borderless and teamLab Planets are permanent museums in other cities, and neither has a Barcelona venue.</p>
+<p><strong>What is the closest thing to teamLab in Barcelona?</strong>
+Moco Museum for an actual teamLab work, SABDA's new immersive show for digital nature in a 360° room, Casa Batlló's Gaudí Cube for large-scale digital art, and Codi Gaudí for interactive VR.</p>
+<p><strong>How much is SABDA's new immersive show?</strong>
+€20 for adults and €12 for children, including a welcome drink. It lasts 25 minutes and runs on Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays.</p>
